# Solidity sources are checked out with CRLF line endings, everywhere.
#
# The metadata hash solc appends to the bytecode covers the source bytes, including their line
# endings. The contracts on both lanes were compiled from this working tree, where the files are
# CRLF, while git stores them as LF — so a Linux clone compiled identical code with a different
# metadata hash, and `npm run check:deployed` failed on CI while passing locally. Pinning the
# endings makes the bytes that produced the on-chain bytecode the bytes every clone gets, which is
# the whole point of a check that claims the build reproduces the deployment.
*.sol text eol=crlf
